.TH KTOOL 1 "October 2026" "ktool 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktool \- Linux kernel development tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktool
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I {build\-cross,build\-kernel,build\-amdgpu\-dkms,fast\-build\-amdgpu,build\-remote,init\-update,stage\-amdgpu,dmabuf\-test,bnxt,man}
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ktool
is a unified CLI for Linux kernel development workflows.
It replaces a collection of bash scripts with a single installable Python
package, providing consistent flag handling, idempotent steps, and
incremental build acceleration via ccache.
.TP
.B build\-cross
Cross-compile a kernel and modules for ARM64 or RISC-V from a local kernel
source tree.
.TP
.B build\-kernel
Clone a remote kernel branch and build Debian or RPM packages.
Preset flags cover the io_uring DMA-BUF, KNOD and p2pdma trees.
.TP
.B build\-amdgpu\-dkms
Stage the amdgpu out-of-tree driver source and build it as a DKMS module
for a specified kernel version.
.TP
.B fast\-build\-amdgpu
Incremental amdgpu OOT build that bypasses DKMS and keeps a persistent
build output directory, cutting warm rebuild times from minutes to seconds.
Optionally runs inside a Docker container.
.TP
.B build\-remote
Pull a running kernel config from a remote host or VM, apply a
.BR localmodconfig ,
optionally apply a config-script fragment, build a kernel package, and
install it.
Must be called from the top level of a kernel source tree.
.TP
.B init\-update
Initialise a kernel git repository with the standard remotes
(Linus, stable, WSL2, lk-library, amdgpu, ubuntu-noble) or update them.
.TP
.B stage\-amdgpu
Download the amdgpu source from a GitHub release tarball and produce the
DKMS source layout that
.B build\-amdgpu\-dkms
and
.B fast\-build\-amdgpu
expect, including autoconf\-generated configure.
No git operations required.
.TP
.B dmabuf\-test
End-to-end DMA-BUF P2P validation: spin up a rocjitsu GPU VM, build and
install the 7.2.x backport kernel, build the amdgpu-dkms module, then run
raw NVMe and XFS filesystem P2P tests.
Parallel amdgpu source copy overlaps kernel build; all stages are
idempotent.
.TP
.B bnxt
Build or install the out-of-tree Broadcom bnxt_en and bnxt_re drivers.
Two sub\-subcommands:
.B build
and
.BR install .
.TP
.B man
Open this man page using the system
.BR man (1)
pager, or fall back to
.BR less (1)
via nroff if man is not available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the ktool version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of subcommands and exit.
Pass
.B \-\-help
after a subcommand name for that subcommand's full flag list.
.SH SUBCOMMAND REFERENCE
.SS build\-cross
.B ktool build\-cross
.RB [ \-\-arch
.IR {arm64,riscv} ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-cross\-tools
.IR PREFIX ]
.RB [ \-\-threads
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.PP
Must be called from the top level of a kernel source tree.
Builds the kernel image, installs modules and headers, then archives them
into a timestamped output directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " {arm64,riscv}"
Target architecture (default:
.IR arm64 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Kernel .config file to use (default:
.IR .config ).
.TP
.BI \-\-cross\-tools " PREFIX"
Cross-compiler prefix (default:
.I aarch64-linux-gnu-
for arm64,
.I riscv64-linux-gnu-
for riscv).
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Parallel build jobs (default: 16).
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Run
.I make clean
before building.
.SS build\-kernel
.B ktool build\-kernel
.RB [ \-\-remote
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-branch
.IR REF ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-patch
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-threads
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-preset\-dmabuf | \-\-preset\-knod | \-\-preset\-p2pdma ]
.PP
Clones a kernel branch and builds
.I deb-pkg
(or
.I rpm-pkg
with
.BR \-\-rpm ).
.TP
.BI \-\-remote " URL"
Kernel git remote (default: kernel.org stable).
.TP
.BI \-\-branch " REF"
Branch or tag to build (default:
.IR v4.14.49 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Kernel .config to use; runs
.I make defconfig
when omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-patch " PATH"
Patch file or directory to apply before building.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Parallel build jobs (default: 8).
.TP
.B \-\-preset\-dmabuf
Use Anuj Gupta's fs-dmabuf-rfc-v11-desc-v2 tree with 128 threads.
.TP
.B \-\-preset\-knod
Use Taehee Yoo's KNOD dev tree (knod-7.2) with 128 threads.
.TP
.B \-\-preset\-p2pdma
Use the stable p2pdma tree with the
.I patches/p2pdma
series and 128 threads.
.SS build\-amdgpu\-dkms
.B ktool build\-amdgpu\-dkms
.B \-\-kernel\-ver
.I VER
.RB [ \-\-amdgpu\-ref
.IR REF ]
.RB [ \-\-build\-src
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-patch\-dirs
.IR DIRS ]
.RB [ \-\-install | \-\-no\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-mkdeb ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.TP
.BI \-\-kernel\-ver " VER"
Target kernel version (required), e.g.
.IR 6.8.0-136-generic .
Kernel headers must be installed at
.IR /lib/modules/VER/build .
.TP
.BI \-\-amdgpu\-ref " REF"
amdgpu git ref to stage from the kernel working tree in
.I ./src
(default:
.IR master ).
Ignored when
.B \-\-build\-src
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-build\-src " DIR"
Pre-staged source directory produced by
.B ktool stage\-amdgpu
or a previous run.
Skips all git operations.
.TP
.BI \-\-patch\-dirs " DIRS"
Colon-separated list of directories whose
.I *.patch
files are applied in sorted order.
.TP
.BR \-\-install " | " \-\-no\-install
Install the built modules (default: install).
.TP
.B \-\-mkdeb
Produce a kernel-independent source
.I .deb
(Architecture: all) for deployment to other hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Re-stage and rebuild even when the output already exists.
.SS fast\-build\-amdgpu
.B ktool fast\-build\-amdgpu
.B \-\-kernel\-ver
.I VER
.RB [ \-\-amdgpu\-ref
.IR REF ]
.RB [ \-\-build\-src
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-build\-out\-base
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-patch\-dirs
.IR DIRS ]
.RB [ \-\-install | \-\-no\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-docker ]
.RB [ \-\-image
.IR IMAGE ]
.PP
Keeps a persistent
.I BUILD_OUT
directory between runs so the kernel build system can reuse unchanged
.I .o
files.
When
.B ccache
is on
.BR PATH ,
it is injected automatically.
Warm builds after a single-line source edit typically complete in under 5s.
.TP
.BI \-\-build\-out\-base " DIR"
Persistent kernel build output directory (default:
.IR ./amdgpu-build-out ).
.TP
.B \-\-docker
Run the build inside the
.I amdgpu-dkms-build
Docker container, using named volumes
.I amdgpu-dkms-ccache
and
.I amdgpu-dkms-buildout
for persistence.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " IMAGE"
Docker image to use when
.B \-\-docker
is set (default:
.IR amdgpu-dkms-build:<kernel-ver> ).
.SS build\-remote
.B ktool build\-remote
.RB [ \-\-remote\-name
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-config\-script
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-label
.IR SUFFIX ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-build ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-wsl\-mode ]
.PP
Must be called from the top level of a kernel source tree.
Pulls the remote host's running kernel config, runs
.BR localmodconfig ,
applies the chosen config-script fragment, builds a kernel deb package,
ships it to the remote, and reboots.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-name " HOST"
SSH hostname of the target (default:
.IR none ,
which skips the SSH fetch and uses the local running config).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " NAME"
Config filename on the remote under
.I /boot/
(e.g.
.IR config-6.8.0-60-generic ).
Auto-detected when omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-script " NAME"
Config fragment to apply:
.BR default ", " amdgpu ", " amdgpu-dkms ", " infiniband ", " nvme-target ", " wsl .
.TP
.BI \-\-label " SUFFIX"
LOCALVERSION suffix appended to the kernel version string.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-build
Stop after the
.I localmodconfig
setup step without running
.IR make .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-install
Build packages but do not ship or install them.
.TP
.B \-\-wsl\-mode
Build a WSL2 kernel targeting the local host.
No remote SSH connection required.
.SS init\-update
.B ktool init\-update
.RB [ \-\-kernel\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-depth
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-skip\-launchpad ]
.RB [ \-\-check\-out ]
.RB [ \-\-add\-remote
.IR NAME
.IR URL ]
.PP
Initialises a kernel git repository at
.I \-\-kernel\-dir
(creating it if absent) with the standard remotes, then fetches from all of
them.
Running a second time is safe: existing remotes are skipped.
.TP
.BI \-\-kernel\-dir " DIR"
Path to the kernel git repository (default:
.IR ./src ).
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " N"
Shallow clone depth (default: 1; use 0 for a full history clone).
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-launchpad
Skip the ubuntu-noble Launchpad remote (useful in CI where Launchpad is slow or blocked).
.TP
.B \-\-check\-out
Check out the latest stable tag after fetching.
Pass a specific branch ref to check out that branch instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-add\-remote " NAME URL"
Add an extra remote.
Repeatable.
.SS stage\-amdgpu
.B ktool stage\-amdgpu
.I ref
.I output_dir
.RB [ \-\-repo
.IR OWNER/REPO ]
.PP
Downloads the amdgpu source for
.I ref
from GitHub (tag first, branch head as fallback) and extracts it into the
DKMS source layout expected by
.B build\-amdgpu\-dkms
and
.BR fast\-build\-amdgpu .
Runs
.BR aclocal ,
.BR autoheader ,
and
.B autoconf
to generate the
.I configure
script required by
.IR pre-build.sh .
.TP
.I ref
amdgpu ref to fetch: a tag (e.g.
.IR rocm-6.2.4 ,
.IR therock-7.14 )
or a branch head.
.TP
.I output_dir
Destination directory for the staged DKMS source tree.
Removed and recreated on each run.
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " OWNER/REPO"
GitHub repository to fetch from (default:
.IR ROCm/amdgpu ).
.SS dmabuf\-test
.B ktool dmabuf\-test
.RB [ \-\-vm\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-ssh\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-kernel\-branch
.IR REF ]
.RB [ \-\-skip\-kernel\-build ]
.RB [ \-\-skip\-dkms ]
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.RB [ \-\-clean\-full ]
.PP
Runs the complete DMA-BUF P2P validation pipeline.
Per-stage timing is printed at the end; all stages are idempotent and
skipped when their outputs already exist.
Requires
.BR oras ,
.BR qemu\-tool ,
.BR docker ,
and kernel build tools.
.TP
.BI \-\-vm\-name " NAME"
Name of the test VM (default:
.IR dmabuf-test ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-port " PORT"
Host SSH port forwarded to the VM (default: 2232).
.TP
.BI \-\-kernel\-branch " REF"
Stable kernel branch or tag to build (default:
.IR v7.2.4 ).
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-kernel\-build
Skip the kernel build stage and use whatever kernel the VM is already running.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-dkms
Skip the amdgpu DKMS build stage.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Remove kernel debs, .config and orig tarballs before running.
.TP
.B \-\-clean\-full
.B \-\-clean
plus the backing qcow2 and VM metadata.
.SS bnxt build
.B ktool bnxt build
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-kdir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-clean | \-\-no\-clean ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.PP
Builds the
.I bnxt_en
and
.I bnxt_re
drivers from source and copies the resulting
.I .ko
files to the current directory.
Picks up
.B ARCH
and
.B CROSS_COMPILE
from the environment for cross-compilation.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Directory containing the
.I bnxt_en/
and
.I bnxt_re/
source subdirectories (default:
.IR ./ ).
.TP
.BI \-\-kdir " DIR"
Kernel build/source directory (default:
.IR /home/users/sbates/kernel/linux-arm64 ).
.TP
.BR \-\-clean " | " \-\-no\-clean
Run
.I make clean
before building (default: clean).
.SS bnxt install
.B ktool bnxt install
.RB [ \-\-bnxt\-en
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-bnxt\-re
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-kernel
.IR VER ]
.PP
Installs pre-built
.I bnxt_en.ko
and
.I bnxt_re.ko
into the running kernel's module tree and runs
.BR depmod .
Must be run as root.
.TP
.BI \-\-bnxt\-en " FILE"
Path to
.I bnxt_en.ko
(default:
.IR ./bnxt_en.ko ).
.TP
.BI \-\-bnxt\-re " FILE"
Path to
.I bnxt_re.ko
(default:
.IR ./bnxt_re.ko ).
.TP
.BI \-\-kernel " VER"
Kernel version string (default: current
.IR "uname \-r" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialise the kernel source tree with standard remotes:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ktool init\-update \-\-kernel\-dir ./src \-\-depth 1 \-\-skip\-launchpad
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build the io_uring DMA-BUF kernel (Anuj's fs-dmabuf v11 tree):
.PP
.RS
.EX
ktool build\-kernel \-\-preset\-dmabuf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Stage amdgpu source from a tarball and build the DKMS module:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ktool stage\-amdgpu therock\-7.14 /tmp/amdgpu\-staged
ktool build\-amdgpu\-dkms \e
    \-\-kernel\-ver $(uname \-r) \e
    \-\-build\-src /tmp/amdgpu\-staged \e
    \-\-no\-install
.EE
.RE
.PP
Incremental amdgpu build (warm builds complete in ~5s):
.PP
.RS
.EX
ktool fast\-build\-amdgpu \e
    \-\-kernel\-ver 6.8.0\-136\-generic \e
    \-\-build\-src /tmp/amdgpu\-staged \e
    \-\-build\-out\-base ./amdgpu\-build\-out \e
    \-\-no\-install
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build a localmodconfig kernel for a remote VM and install it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ktool build\-remote \e
    \-\-remote\-name my\-test\-vm \e
    \-\-config\-script default \e
    \-\-label \-my\-feature
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./src/
Default location for the kernel git working tree, populated by
.BR "ktool init\-update" .
.TP
.I ~/.ccache/
ccache cache directory used by
.B fast\-build\-amdgpu
and
.BR dmabuf\-test .
Set
.B CCACHE_DIR
to override.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qemu-tool/images/
Default VM image directory used by
.BR dmabuf\-test .
Set
.B VM_IMAGES_DIR
to override.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dkms/
DKMS module tree written by
.BR build\-amdgpu\-dkms .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1),
.BR dkms (8),
.BR qemu\-tool (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephen Bates
